      "source": [
        "# Immortal\n",
        "\n",
        "In CPython, an immortal object is an object whose reference count is not normally changed by reference counting, so it is not deallocated through ordinary reference-count updates.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-immortal)"
      ]
    }
  ],
